From 2681695a04c681310b22c7884797fdfeda0d554e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vincent Leon <leon@mbp.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 23:47:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(push): let a provider push while someone is present

The daemon pushes only when nobody has used Paseo for three minutes;
otherwise the most recently active client gets the alert in-app and no
push goes out. Someone working at a desktop never hears about an alert
on their phone.

A push provider can now declare deliversWhilePresent. When a present
client gets an alert in-app, and nobody is looking at its agent or
terminal, the daemon also pushes through those providers, leaving out
that client's own registration so the device showing the alert does
not get it twice. Without such a provider nothing changes: senders
that lack sendWhilePresent, as the tests' recording sender does, keep
the old rule exactly.

The Huawei provider declares it by default. "pushWhilePresent": false
in huawei-push/options.json restores the push-only-when-away rule.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
